  "response_text": "Here are the kinds of tasks I can help you with, based on the tools available on this MCP server:\n\n- **Server/tool administration** — list tools, read tool metadata, register tools, update tool metadata, abort tool registrations, get server info.\n- **Knowledge base** — retrieve entries, write/update entries, compose answers from retrieved entries.\n- **Authorization** — decide whether an action is allowed for a subject.\n- **General information** — current time for a timezone, weather, and temperature for a city.\n- **Robot/system state & perception** — read robot state, perceive the scene, read lidar, capture visual scenes.\n- **Planning & control** — plan actions, decode action chunks, consume instructions, emit control commands, publish ROS2/twist topics, execute manipulation and physical actions.\n\nSteps I would take for the task I was given (reviewing the tools registered on the MCP server and reporting their current state), in order:\n\n1. Call `get_server_info` to get the server name, version, and the number of tools registered and approved.\n2. Call `list_tools` to enumerate every registered tool and its approval status.\n3. For each tool returned by `list_tools`, call `read_tool_metadata` to read its registered definition (name, description, schema, and approval status).\n4. Consolidate the results into a report showing each tool's current state.\n5. Present that report to you.",
